    {
      "id": "REV.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this I beheld, and lo, a great multitude, which no man could number, of all nations, and kindreds, and people, and languages, stood before the throne, and before the Lamb, clothed with white robes, and palms in their hands;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And cried with a loud voice, saying, Salvation to our God who sitteth upon the throne, and to the Lamb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all the angels stood around the throne, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "about",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the elders and the four living beings, and fell before the throne on their faces, and worshiped God,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Saying, Amen: Blessing, and glory, and wisdom, and thanksgiving, and honor, and power, and might, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to our God for ever and ever. Amen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And one of the elders answered, saying to me, Who are these that are arrayed in white robes? and whence came they?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I said to him, Sir, thou knowest. And he said to me, These are they who came out of great tribulation, and have washed their robes, and made them white in the blood of the Lamb.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore they are before the throne of God, and serve him day and night in his temple: and he that sitteth on the throne will dwell among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall hunger no more, neither thirst any more; neither shall the sun light on them, nor any heat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "REV.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:REV.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the Lamb who is in the midst of the throne will feed them, and will lead them to living fountains of waters: and God will wipe away all tears from their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
